  "_README": [
    "Parity fixtures: Go-computed values must match Python POC values within 1e-9.",
    "INPUTS below are pre-populated. EXPECTED fields are null (or empty string) until you fill them in.",
    "",
    "How to populate:",
    "  1. Run the Python POC with the same inputs given in each scenario.",
    "  2. Record Python's outputs in the 'expected' block of that scenario.",
    "  3. Run: go test -v ./validation/...",
    "  4. Test passes only when every populated value matches Go within tolerance.",
    "",
    "Tolerance: 1e-9 for float64; byte-identical hex strings for SHA-256.",
    "If you populate a value and the test fails, the diff and both sides are reported.",
    "",
    "Sentinel: null means 'not yet populated' for floats; empty string for hashes.",
    "Both pass through with a log line — they never fail the test."
